  "findings": [
    "Kept actual Engine binding-conflict behavior; transient lifecycle tests use their own object.",
    "Preserved capture-denial CLI wording while extending the authority scope through PNG output.",
    "Incremental fixture reuse now updates existing integration directories instead of failing FileExists.",
    "Trace retains complete static catalog name literals.",
    "Openas grant-scope conformance requires animation.seek-progress; the C++ method remains seek_progress."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Native typed adapter, not a new wire schema/RPC server, transport authentication layer or generic provider registry.",
    "Controller borrows Engine/context and requires serial calls and correct host lifetime; no background execution or async cancellation.",
    "Contexts do not implicitly cross instance/type boundaries; UI compatibility conversion and operation-policy mapping remain host work.",
    "Native callers are trusted; transport hosts bind actor/session/remote metadata. In-process limited Agent work must carry delegated authority too.",
    "Dry-run is admission preview, not domain validation or simulated execution; no automatic undo journal or per-object resource ACL.",
    "Scripted native Agent-role verification is not an external LLM or online interoperability acceptance.",
    "No new website layout or browser/delivery performance measurement; complete 40/20 and global architecture requirements remain open."
  ]
